sale of natural gas in Kentucky and Rhode Island; sale of wholesale electricity in Kentucky; and generation of electricity from power plants in Kentucky. It generates electricity from coal, gas, hydro, and solar sources. The company was formerly known as PP&L Resources, Inc. and changed its name to PPL Corporation in 2000. PPL Corporation was founded in 1920 and is headquartered in Allentown, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vincent  Sorgi CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["PPL Corporation is a large-cap utilities business with a $26.6B market cap on $9.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $1.4B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{